      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): invalidate stale roleRefs on main-frame navigation",
        "body": "Closes: N/A (source-first bug fix)\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where browser role refs (`e1`, `e2`, …) from a snapshot taken on page A could resolve to wrong elements on page B after a main-frame navigation. Three cached fields were stale after navigation: `state.roleRefs`, `state.roleRefsMode`/`state.roleRefsFrameSelector`, and the cross-Page `roleRefsByTarget` cache.\n\nAdditionally, the v1 fix stored navigation generation per-`PageState`, but `roleRefsByTarget` is intentionally shared across replacement `Page` objects. A replacement Page starting at generation zero could restore stale pre-navigation refs or reject fresh post-navigation refs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n1. **framenavigated listener** clears `roleRefs`/`roleRefsMode`/`roleRefsFrameSelector` on main-frame navigation\n2. **Target-scoped navGen** (`navGenerationByTarget` map keyed by `cdpUrl+targetId`) shared across replacement Pages via `pageTargetKeys` WeakMap\n3. **Eviction** of `navGenerationByTarget` entries alongside `roleRefsByTarget` eviction (prevents unbounded map growth)\n4. **restore guard** compares cached navGen with current target generation\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Stale refs after navigation throw \"Unknown ref\" instead of silently clicking wrong elements\n- Replacement Page objects correctly share navigation lifecycle\n- No impact on subframe navigations, page close, or existing workflows\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n### Real Chrome/CDP proof (Google Chrome 138 + Playwright CDP)\n```\nReal Chrome/CDP proof: roleRefs invalidation on navigation\n\n[phase 1] Snapshot on Page A\n  Page A loaded: file:///tmp/.../page-a.html\n  ok: refLocator resolves e1 on page A\n\n[phase 2] Navigate to Page B\n  Page B loaded: file:///tmp/.../page-b.html\n  ok: FIXED: refLocator throws Unknown ref after navigation (stale ref rejected)\n  ok: FIXED: refLocator throws Unknown ref for e2 too\n\n[phase 3] Fresh snapshot on Page B\n  ok: fresh snapshot stores refs on Page B\n\n[phase 4] Replacement Page (new Page for same target)\n  ok: replacement Page restores refs for same target\n\n[phase 5] Navigate back to Page A\n  ok: FIXED: refs cleared after second navigation\n  ok: re-snapshot after second navigation works\n\nEnvironment: Google Chrome 138 + Playwright CDP\nALL REAL CHROME PROOF ASSERTIONS: 7 passed, 0 failed\n```\n\n### Synthetic proof (real production functions + fake Page events): 21/21\nProof covers role-mode clear, aria-mode clear, frameSelector clear, subframe preserve, close cleanup, re-snapshot, navGen guard, replacement-Page stale reject, replacement-Page fresh restore.\n\n### Negative control (per-PageState navGen reverted): 20/21\nConfirmed v1 defect: replacement Page restores stale gen-0 cache after target navigation.\n\n### Vitest: 91 passed (5 files)\n37 tests in pw-session.test.ts (4 replacement-Page scenarios, navGen eviction coverage)\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Real Chrome/CDP:** 7 assertions across 5 phases — navigation, stale rejection, fresh snapshot, replacement Page, second navigation\n- **Synthetic:** 21/21 positive, 20/21 negative control (v1 defect confirmed)\n- **Lint:** clean (`node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs`)\n- **Format:** clean (`npx oxfmt --write`)\n- CI all green\n",
        "branch": "fix/browser-stale-rolerefs-navigation",
